- **Method visibility.** The interceptor must be able to see the method. Public is the safe default; Kotlin `internal`/final classes need the proxy to be able to subclass, so keep classes non-final (or use interface-based proxies / enable class-proxy-friendly settings). A Kotlin class is final by default — this is a common trap: mark the class or method `open` (the `kotlin-spring` / `allopen` plugin handles this for `@Service`-annotated classes, but verify the project actually enables it).
